  "One geometry paper, copied exactly, sent out to be marked. The first teacher gave it 70.": "一份几何试卷，被原样复制后寄出评分。第一位老师给了70分。",
  "In 1913 two researchers took a real geometry final, written by a pupil in a large Wisconsin high school, and had printing plates made of it so that hundreds of copies reproduced the original in every detail, handwriting and all. Every marker therefore saw the identical script: the same proofs, the same crossings out, the same untidy diagrams. Five geometry teachers in the pupil's own school each marked that script independently, without conferring. They share a staffroom, a syllabus, and one written passing grade, which is 70. The first of them marked it exactly 70, so on that marker's desk the paper passed, with nothing to spare.": "1913年，两位研究者拿来一份真实的几何期末试卷，出自威斯康星州一所大中学的学生之手，并制作了印刷版，让几百份复制件在每一个细节上都与原件一致，连笔迹也不例外。因此每一位评卷人看到的都是同一份试卷：同样的证明、同样的涂改、同样潦草的图形。这名学生所在学校的五位几何老师各自独立评阅了这份试卷，彼此没有商量。他们共用一间教师办公室、一套教学大纲，以及唯一一条写明的及格线，就是70分。其中第一位给了整整70分，所以在这位评卷人的桌上，试卷及格了，而且一分余地也没有。",
  "The other four teachers in that same school marked the identical script. What did their marks do to the verdict?": "同一所学校的另外四位老师评阅了这份一模一样的试卷。他们的分数让这个结果发生了什么变化？",
  "Marks given to one geometry script": "给同一份几何试卷打出的分数",
  "One geometry final, reproduced by plate so every marker saw the identical script": "一份几何期末试卷，由印刷版复制，使每位评卷人看到的都是同一份试卷",
  "Mark out of 100": "百分制分数",
  "The school's passing grade, 70": "该校的及格线，70",
